  "description": "FACTEM crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C150 H115 O25 Yb5,4(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb1A (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb1B (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb1C (Yb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.514-4.969 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.52-156.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Yb5(μ4-OH)(μ3-OH)4(μ-η2-Ph2acac)4(η2-DBM)6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
